<main>
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
 <div class="hero-text">
  <p class="status"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>In development. The first build will appear on GitHub.</p>
  <h1>Phone gestures for everyday actions</h1>
  <p class="lead">Shake the phone for the flashlight, flip it face down for silence, tap the back to pause music. Tukk recognizes gestures on the phone itself and runs the action right away.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/vkardin/tukk">Follow on GitHub</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#gestures">See all gestures</a></div>
  <p class="meta">Android 8.0 and later. No internet access, no accounts, no data collection.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="demo">
  <div class="stage" role="img" aria-label="Tukk demo: a phone that reacts to gestures">
   <div class="beam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
   <div class="phone">
    <div class="screen">
     <div class="bar"><span class="clock">21:30</span><span class="icons"><svg class="bell" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 16V11a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v5l2 2H4z"/><path d="M10 20a2 2 0 0 0 4 0"/><path class="slash" d="M4 4l16 16"/></svg></span></div>
     <svg class="ember" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#ff7a35" d="M24,3 L42,13 L45,32 L29,44 L9,39 L3,21 Z"/><path fill="#1b1715" d="M24,5 L23,20 L6,20 Z M24,6 L39,14 L26,20 Z M5,23 L21,23 L10,36 Z M12,37 L23,25 L29,41 Z M28,23 L40,16 L42,31 L31,39 Z"/><path fill="#ffd9a0" d="M24,9 L25,20 L37,15 L27,23 L31,37 L24,25 L13,35 L21,23 L9,21 L23,21 Z"/></svg>
     <div class="toast" aria-hidden="true"></div>
     <div class="track"><span class="cover" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><b>Evening playlist</b><small>On the phone</small></span><span class="pp" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
    </div>
    <span class="ripple" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ripple r2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p class="try" id="try-label">Try a gesture</p>
  <div class="gestures" role="group" aria-labelledby="try-label"><button type="button" class="gesture" data-gesture="shake" data-on="Flashlight on" data-off="Flashlight off" aria-pressed="false">Shake</button><button type="button" class="gesture" data-gesture="tap" data-on="Music paused" data-off="Music playing" aria-pressed="false">Tap the back</button><button type="button" class="gesture" data-gesture="flip" data-on="Silent mode on" data-off="Sound back on" aria-pressed="false">Face down</button><button type="button" class="gesture" data-gesture="chop" data-on="SOS signal on" data-off="SOS signal off" aria-pressed="false">Chop twice</button></div>
  <p class="result" role="status" aria-live="polite">Pick a gesture to see what happens.</p>
 </div>
</div></section>

<section id="gestures" class="block"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Five gestures, each with its own action</h2><p class="sub">Every gesture gets its own action, sensitivity, cooldown and conditions.</p>
 <ul class="glist"><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6v12M15 6v12" /><path d="M5 9l-2 3 2 3M19 9l2 3-2 3"/></svg><div><b>Shake</b><p>Shake the phone sharply twice.</p></div></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 17l5-10M12 17l5-10"/><path d="M4 20h16"/></svg><div><b>Chop</b><p>Two quick chopping motions, like Motorola's chop-chop.</p></div></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="3" width="10" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="1.6"/><circle cx="12" cy="15" r="1.6"/></svg><div><b>Back tap</b><p>Two or three taps on the back, calibrated for your phone and case.</p></div></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="13" width="16" height="6" rx="2"/><path d="M12 4v6M9 7l3 3 3-3"/></svg><div><b>Face down</b><p>Turn the phone over onto its screen.</p></div></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="8" y="3" width="8" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M19 7v3M19 13v3"/></svg><div><b>Volume buttons</b><p>Press a volume button twice, or up then down. Needs optional accessibility access.</p></div></li></ul>
</div></section>

<section id="features" class="block"><div class="wrap split">
 <div><h2>What a gesture can do</h2><p class="sub">Repeat the gesture to switch back: shake again and the flashlight turns off.</p></div>
 <ul class="acts"><li>Flashlight with adjustable strength</li><li>SOS signal</li><li>Silent and vibrate modes</li><li>Sound on</li><li>Play and pause</li><li>Next and previous track</li><li>Open any app</li><li>Camera</li><li>Voice recorder</li><li>Screenshot</li></ul>
</div></section>

<section class="block"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Built to stay out of the way</h2>
 <div class="whys"><div class="why"><h3>Instant</h3><p>Gestures are recognized on the phone itself, and the action runs right away.</p></div><div class="why"><h3>Light on battery</h3><p>Only the sensors your gestures need are on. With the screen off they are read in batches.</p></div><div class="why"><h3>No accidental triggers</h3><p>Pocket detection, cooldowns, pauses during calls and charging, and a live test for every gesture.</p></div><div class="why"><h3>Private</h3><p>No internet permission, no accounts, no analytics. Settings stay on the phone.</p></div></div>
</div></section>

<section id="privacy" class="block"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Asks only for what it needs</h2>
 <div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Permission</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Notifications</th><td>Shows that gestures are active, with Pause and Settings buttons.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Do Not Disturb access</th><td>Only for the silent, vibrate and sound actions.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Accessibility, optional</th><td>Volume button gestures, screenshots and opening apps directly. Tukk never reads screen content.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div></section>

<section id="status" class="block"><div class="wrap">
 <div class="soon">
  <svg class="soon-mark" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#ff7a35" d="M24,3 L42,13 L45,32 L29,44 L9,39 L3,21 Z"/><path fill="#1b1715" d="M24,5 L23,20 L6,20 Z M24,6 L39,14 L26,20 Z M5,23 L21,23 L10,36 Z M12,37 L23,25 L29,41 Z M28,23 L40,16 L42,31 L31,39 Z"/><path fill="#ffd9a0" d="M24,9 L25,20 L37,15 L27,23 L31,37 L24,25 L13,35 L21,23 L9,21 L23,21 Z"/></svg>
  <div><h2>Tukk is in development</h2><p>The first build will appear in GitHub Releases, with a Google Play listing later. Follow the repository to hear when it is out.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/vkardin/tukk">Open the repository</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/vkardin/tukk/issues">Suggest an idea or report a bug</a></div></div>
 </div>
</div></section>

<section id="faq" class="block"><div class="wrap narrow">
 <h2>Questions</h2>
 <div class="faq"><details><summary>Does it work with the screen off?</summary><p>Yes. Each gesture can work with the screen on, off or both. With the screen off, sensors are read in batches to save battery.</p></details><details><summary>Will it go off in my pocket?</summary><p>Pocket detection, cooldowns and pauses during calls or charging keep accidental triggers away. Each gesture has a live test to tune its sensitivity.</p></details><details><summary>Why would it ask for accessibility access?</summary><p>Only for volume button gestures, screenshots and opening apps directly. It is optional, and Tukk never reads screen content.</p></details><details><summary>My phone stops it in the background.</summary><p>Settings, then Background work, has steps for Xiaomi, Samsung, Huawei, OnePlus and other phones.</p></details></div>
</div></section>

